{
  "id": "trade-please-dp",
  "name": "Trade Please DP",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "Trade Please DP (とりかえっこDP) was a card swap run in Japan from January 2007 to August 2008: players handed over a Pokémon card of their own, even an old yellow-bordered card or one with the old card back, and got a promo in return, without choosing which, while stocks lasted; Trainer and Energy cards could not be swapped. It began at the 25th Next Generation World Hobby Fair, in Osaka, Tokyo, Nagoya and Fukuoka in January and February 2007, and at official gym events those months, with eight cards: Turtwig, Chimchar, Piplup, Pachirisu, Mime Jr., Staravia, Buneary and Glameow. They came back at the Gym Challenge tournaments held to launch the Secret of the Lakes expansion, where every player got some for each match, win or lose.\n\nThe later rounds gave holo cards, one swap per person. From 8 July 2007 shops such as Jusco, Ito-Yokado and Toys\"R\"Us gave Cherrim, Pikachu, Luxio, Toxicroak and Lopunny, and Pokémon Centers the middle-stage starters Grotle, Monferno and Prinplup; from 4 November 2007 card shops gave Burmy, Shellos, Shinx, Murkrow and Eevee, and Pokémon Centers Magmar, Electabuzz and Riolu. The last rounds were part of the summer 2008 Collection Challenge, and asked for holo cards in exchange: one for Pichu from 19 July, and two for Buneary and Lopunny together in August.",
